p.src:
Let $P_{\mathrm{client}}$ denote the client’s pain point, failure risk, or unsolved need. The sales process Williams describes has the following order: $\mathrm{Homework}
\longrightarrow
P_{\mathrm{client}}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Questions}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{True\ Need}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Solution}.$ The product appears late in the chain. Young salespeople, in his telling, often begin with a demo and hope something catches. Williams wants the opposite order: do the homework before the meeting, ask questions first, and use the product only after the need has been found.

