As a mnemonic, we can write career capital as $K_{\mathrm{career}}
=
K_{\mathrm{skills}}
+
K_{\mathrm{relationships}}
+
K_{\mathrm{reputation}}.$ This is not a transcript equation. It is a compact way to keep Williams’s three-part claim from dissolving into a slogan. Skills matter. People matter. The reputation formed by helping people get better also matters.

