p.src:
This closing advice is not disconnected from the earlier mechanics. It is the same trust mechanism moved into career form. Helping others creates trust; trust creates access; access creates chances to learn, sell, invest, and lead. A compact version is $\mathrm{Help}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Trust}
\longrightarrow
\mathrm{Opportunity}
\longrightarrow
K_{\mathrm{career}}.$ Williams warns that the more one is by oneself, the more one will be by oneself. That is not just moral advice. It is a network claim. Careers compound through other people.

